/--
Outside the adaptive selected-shell partition certificate, the source-shell
transport proof supplies the raw empirical-`W₁` threshold used by the PZ RGD
perturbation bound.  The finite-head comparison is kept explicit because it
is the dimensional schedule bridge, not part of the certificate itself.
-/
theorem empiricalWassersteinOne_le_of_not_pOneFournierGuillinAdaptiveEuclideanSelectedShellPartitionCertificate
    (dimension cutoff : ℕ) (eta alpha gamma momentBound deviation : ℝ)
    (confidence : ℕ → ℝ) (countSchedule : ℕ → ℕ)
    (hcountPositive : ∀ round, 0 < countSchedule round)
    (law : ∀ iteration,
      HeterogeneousBatchTrace (fun round => Fin (countSchedule round))
        (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin dimension)) iteration →
        ProbabilityMeasure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin dimension)))
