If the conditional IID uniform-risk failure at round `t` is assigned the
source's `6 p / (pi^2 (t + 1)^2)` budget, every finite adaptive prefix succeeds
with probability at least `1 - p`.  The paper's sample-size/concentration
argument that establishes those per-round bounds is intentionally not assumed
here.
