/--
Arbitrary-law compact-convex existence for Proposition 4.1.  This follows
the arXiv Appendix D.5 best-response/Kakutani structure.  It takes joint
decoupled-risk continuity directly, so it does not claim the still-open
source bridge from Wasserstein continuity of the law map to that premise.
-/
theorem exists_isMeasurePerformativelyStableOn_of_compact_convex
    {Parameter Data : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup Parameter] [NormedSpace ℝ Parameter]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ Parameter] [MeasurableSpace Data]
    (model : MeasurePerformativeModel Parameter Data) (domain : Set Parameter)
    (hcompact : IsCompact domain) (hne : domain.Nonempty) (hconvex : Convex ℝ domain)
    (hjoint : Continuous (fun point : Parameter × Parameter =>
      measureDecoupledPerformativeRisk model point.1 point.2))
    (hfrozenConvex : ∀ deployed : domain,
      ConvexOn ℝ domain (fun candidate =>
        measureDecoupledPerformativeRisk model deployed.1 candidate)) :
    ∃ parameter ∈ domain, IsMeasurePerformativelyStableOn model domain parameter := by
  obtain ⟨fixed, hfixed⟩ := kakutani_fixed_point domain hconvex hcompact hne
    (measurePerformativeBestResponseOn model domain)
    (closedGraph_measurePerformativeBestResponseOn_of_compact model domain hcompact hjoint)
    (fun deployed => ⟨fun _candidate hcandidate => hcandidate.1,
      convex_measurePerformativeBestResponseOn model domain hfrozenConvex deployed,
      measurePerformativeBestResponseOn_nonempty_of_compact model domain hcompact hne hjoint deployed⟩)
  exact ⟨fixed.1, fixed.2, hfixed⟩

/--
The loss-convexity form of arbitrary-law Proposition 4.1 existence.  It
derives the frozen-risk convexity required by the Kakutani route by integrating
the pointwise source loss condition.
